sxml check - Check that XML documents are well-formed

Usage: sxml check [--external-entities] [--validate-dtd] [--format=FORMAT] FILE...

Checks that each FILE is a well-formed XML 1.0 or XML 1.1 document
(by the version its XML declaration names) that also conforms to
Namespaces in XML. No tree is built. The supported encodings are
UTF-8, UTF-16, ISO-8859-1 and US-ASCII. The external DTD subset and
external entities are read only with --external-entities, and then
only as local files, relative to the file that refers to them.

With --validate-dtd, each FILE must also be valid against its DTD
(XML 1.0, section 5.1); the first error of each FILE is reported. A
FILE without a document type declaration is not valid. An external
DTD subset is part of the DTD only with --external-entities.

Prints nothing when every FILE is well-formed (valid). Each problem is
reported on standard error as
  FILE:LINE:COLUMN: message
With --format=json, one JSON object on standard output lists every
FILE with its "status".

Exit status: 0 when every FILE is well-formed (valid), 1 when one is
not, 3 when one cannot be read.

Options:
  -h, --help               Show this help and exit
      --external-entities  Read the external DTD subset and external entities as local files
      --validate-dtd       Also check that each FILE is valid against its DTD
      --format=FORMAT      Report format (one of: text, json; default: text)

Arguments:
  FILE  XML document to check; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml check books.xml
  sxml check --format=json books.xml broken.xml
  sxml check --validate-dtd --external-entities article.xml
